{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2175-10-06 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be your oncologist during this admission. You’re here for your 11th cycle of high-dose methotrexate for your CNS lymphoma, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2175-10-06 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. It’s been a month since the last one. I’m trying to stay on track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2175-10-06 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great sticking with the schedule. We’ll start the infusion around noon. First, I want to check in—how have you been feeling overall?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2175-10-06 11:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Honestly, I’ve been struggling a bit emotionally. I’ve been crying a lot, even when nothing’s really wrong. It’s hard to keep going with all these treatments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2175-10-06 11:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m really sorry you’re feeling that way. That’s not uncommon with long-term treatment. We can get you support. Would it be okay if we had the psychiatry team come talk to you?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2175-10-06 11:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, please. I’ve never seen a psychiatrist before, but I think I need help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2175-10-06 11:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll arrange that. They’ll help with coping strategies and possibly medication. Also, any new physical symptoms? Headaches, weakness?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2175-10-06 11:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No new headaches. My balance feels a little off sometimes, but it’s not worse than usual. And my foot pain is still there—burning, goes up my leg."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2175-10-06 11:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, that’s good—no worsening neurologically. We’ll keep you on gabapentin for the nerve pain. You mentioned stopping it before?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2175-10-06 11:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I tried stopping it, but the pain came back badly at night. I restarted it right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2175-10-06 11:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good call. We might even increase the dose later if needed. Now, we’re going to give you IV fluids with bicarbonate to protect your kidneys during chemo. You’ll also get anti-nausea meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2175-10-06 11:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I usually get nauseous the next day. Is that still expected?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2175-10-06 11:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, some nausea is common. We’ll have ondansetron ready for you. You’ll also start leucovorin tomorrow to help clear the methotrexate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2175-10-06 11:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my asthma? I had a little wheezing a few days ago."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2175-10-06 11:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your lung exam is clear today. Keep using your fluticasone-salmeterol and montelukast. Use albuterol if you wheeze. We’ll monitor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2175-10-06 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re starting the methotrexate infusion now. It’ll take a few hours. Nurses will check your vitals regularly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2175-10-06 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel a bit flushed. Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2175-10-06 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s common. We’re watching you closely. Any headache or nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2175-10-06 14:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Not yet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2175-10-06 16:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well with the infusion. Now we’re sending you for an MRI to check your brain. It’s routine to make sure the lymphoma is still stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2175-10-06 18:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The MRI is back. Good news—no new tumors or changes. The surgical area looks stable, and no signs of progression."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2175-10-06 18:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2175-10-06 18:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep monitoring. The psychiatry team will come by tomorrow morning to talk with you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2175-10-07 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How’s your night been? Any nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2175-10-07 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little nauseous this morning. I took the ondansetron."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2175-10-07 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s expected. It should improve. The psychiatrist reviewed your case. They recommend starting an antidepressant—citalopram, 10 mg daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2175-10-07 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that safe with the chemo?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2175-10-07 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s safe. We’ll start it now and increase to 20 mg when you’re discharged. They also recommend therapy. Social work is helping set that up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2175-10-07 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been drinking a little wine to cope. Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2175-10-07 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m glad you told me. Alcohol can worsen liver irritation from methotrexate. It’s best to avoid it, especially now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2175-10-07 09:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t realize. I’ll stop."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2175-10-07 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. The team also suggested not using lorazepam if you’re anxious, due to your family history with alcohol."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2175-10-07 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs this morning show your liver enzymes are up—ALT 58, AST 42. That’s expected with methotrexate. We’ll keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2175-10-07 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2175-10-07 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not usually. It goes up after each cycle and comes back down. We adjust your leucovorin to help protect your liver."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2175-10-07 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My foot pain is worse at night. Can we do anything?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2175-10-07 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re considering increasing your gabapentin to 900 mg three times a day, especially to help you sleep. We’ll discuss that before discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2175-10-08 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your methotrexate level is down to 0.05, which means your body is clearing it well. That’s great news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2175-10-08 08:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Does that mean I can go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2175-10-08 08:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, likely tomorrow. Your liver numbers are improving, no nausea today, and your mood support is set up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2175-10-08 08:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m worried about money. I can’t work, and insurance is so expensive."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2175-10-08 08:53:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. Social work is looking into disability options and financial aid programs for you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2175-10-08 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve approved increasing your gabapentin to 900 mg three times a day after discharge. Take it with food to avoid stomach upset."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2175-10-08 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the citalopram?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2175-10-08 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take 20 mg daily starting tomorrow. It may take a few weeks to feel the full effect. Keep your therapy appointment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2175-10-08 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel better already knowing I have support."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2175-10-08 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s wonderful to hear. We’re also arranging a referral to an outpatient therapist near you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2175-10-09 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All your labs are stable. You’re cleared to go home. You’ll continue enoxaparin for blood clots, your asthma meds, and levetiracetam."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2175-10-09 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And when’s my next chemo?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2175-10-09 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "In one month. You’ll need to do your 24-hour urine collection before coming in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2175-10-09 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll be ready. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2175-10-09 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing an amazing job. Keep in touch with your team, take your meds, and call if anything changes. You’ve got this."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2175-10-06 10:35:00",
    "admission_end": "2175-10-09 14:50:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 50-year-old woman with primary central nervous system lymphoma, ulcerative colitis, asthma, and a history of DVT/PE was admitted for her 11th cycle of high-dose methotrexate chemotherapy. She tolerated the treatment well, with expected transaminitis that resolved and manageable nausea. An MRI showed stable disease with no evidence of progression. She reported ongoing depressive symptoms, leading to a psychiatry consultation, initiation of citalopram, and referral for outpatient therapy. Social work was engaged to address financial stressors and disability resources. Her chronic right foot pain was reassessed, and gabapentin was uptitrated for better nocturnal control. She cleared methotrexate adequately and was discharged home in stable condition with plans to continue enoxaparin, resume mesalamine, and follow up with oncology in one month for the next cycle.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Primary central nervous system lymphoma, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Headache",
      "Mononeuritis of lower limb, unspecified",
      "Personal history of venous thrombosis and embolism",
      "Personal history of pulmonary embolism",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Nausea with vomiting",
      "Antineoplastic and immunosuppressive drugs causing adverse effects in therapeutic use"
    ]
  }
}
